@methods: bequest
# The methods of the terminal stage as an addition to
# applications/retirement-choice/declaration/stages/bequest/bequest.bl: the
# derivative of the terminal value in wealth, zero, as an authored line of the
# decision value builder, from marginals_bequest.bl. The block restates the
# partial signature of that file's block dcsn_marginal, () -> (V) : !dcsn: by
# rule 4 the empty domain side adds nothing, and the codomain's coordinate V,
# equal by name to the stage's and carrying no classifier, adds none, while
# its perch word !dcsn agrees with the stage's, so the union's signature is the
# stage's. The stage takes no method: its values are closed forms.

[id=cntn_to_dcsn, () -> (V) : !dcsn] {
    D_{x}V = 0                                         :: [id=marginal_wealth]
}
